.TH POMODORO-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-17" "pomodoro-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pomodoro-revamped \- a Pomodoro timer in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pomodoro-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pomodoro-revamped
runs a Pomodoro timer whose whole state lives in tmux options, so it survives
a detach and writes no file. It stores the second the timer started and the
seconds it spent paused, and every render derives the phase and the time left
from them. The entry point
.B pomodoro-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the toggle key and every other
key that is set, in one tmux call, and replaces the placeholder
#{pomodoro_status} in status-left and status-right with a call to
.BR status .
.PP
A round is work periods separated by short breaks and closed by a long break.
When a phase ends, the render that notices it first claims the change with
one conditional tmux command, so several clients count one work period, run
the hooks once and send one notification.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the keys and replace the status placeholder now.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B toggle
Start the timer when it is idle, pause it when it runs, resume it when it is paused.
.TP
.B skip
Jump to the next phase. An idle timer is left alone.
.TP
.B restart
Start the current phase again from its whole length. An idle timer is left alone.
.TP
.B cancel
Stop the timer and clear what it published.
.TP
.B status
Print the status segment, and count a phase that just ended. The status line runs it.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the notifier, less, the keys it found bound, gum and the core tools. Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-work
or
.BR \-\-show\-progress .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on every binding and on the status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI POMODORO_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR POMODORO_REVAMPED_WORK .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B POMODORO_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B POMODORO_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B POMODORO_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B POMODORO_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_toggle_key
The prefix key that starts, pauses or resumes the timer. off binds nothing. The default is M\-s, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_cancel_key
The prefix key that cancels the timer. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_skip_key
The prefix key that skips to the next phase. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_restart_key
The prefix key that restarts the current phase. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_menu_key
The prefix key that opens a menu of start or pause, skip, restart and cancel. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_help_key
The prefix key that opens the help page in a popup, in less, or whole where less is not installed. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_work
Minutes of a work period. The default is 25.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_break
Minutes of a short break. The default is 5.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_long_break
Minutes of the long break that ends a round. The default is 15.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_intervals
Work periods in a round, before the long break. The default is 4, and 100 at most.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_notify
1 sends a desktop notification when a phase changes and at the warning. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_bell
1 rings the bell of every attached terminal when a phase changes. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_warn_seconds
Above 0, warn once this many seconds before a phase ends. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_quiet_hours
A window such as 22:00\-08:00 in which no bell rings and no notification is sent. Hooks still run. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_goal
Work periods wanted per day, shown with show_goal. The default is 6.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_show_progress
1 draws a progress bar before the time. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_show_interval
0 hides the counter such as [2/4]. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_show_goal
1 shows today's work periods over the goal. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_show_finish
1 shows the time of day the phase ends. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_progress_width
Cells of the progress bar. The default is 8, and 200 at most.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_bar_filled
The filled cell of the progress bar. The default is #.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_bar_empty
The empty cell of the progress bar. The default is \-.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_pause_text
What follows the time while the timer is paused. The default is a space and the word paused.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_work_color
The tmux style of a work period. The default is #[fg=red].
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_break_color
The tmux style of a short break. The default is #[fg=green].
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_long_break_color
The tmux style of the long break. The default is #[fg=blue].
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_work_icon
An icon shown before a work period. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_break_icon
An icon shown before a short break. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_long_break_icon
An icon shown before the long break. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_on_work
A command tmux runs in the background when a work period starts. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_on_break
A command tmux runs in the background when a short break starts. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_on_long_break
A command tmux runs in the background when the long break starts. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_on_cycle
A command tmux runs in the background when a whole round ends, with the long break. The default is none.
.TP
.B @pomodoro_revamped_on_warn
A command tmux runs in the background at the warning. The default is none.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The timer keeps its state in
.BR @pomodoro_revamped_state ,
.BR _start ,
.BR _paused_total ,
.BR _paused_at ,
.BR _last_phase ,
.BR _warned ,
.BR _week_counts ,
.B _week_day
and
.BR _transition_claim .
While it runs,
.B status
also publishes
.BR @pomodoro_revamped_status ,
the segment,
.BR _phase ,
.BR _remaining ,
the seconds left,
.BR _fraction ,
the percent done,
.BR _week ,
the week's work periods as a sparkline, and
.BR _today ,
today's count, for a theme to read.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR less (1),
.BR gum (1)
